From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:19:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] qapi: a weak default panda_handle_qmp, so the tools link on
 macOS

qmp-dispatch.c declared the QMP hook as an undefined weak reference and
tested it for NULL. ELF allows that. Mach-O's ld64 refuses it, so
qemu-img, qemu-io, qemu-nbd and qemu-storage-daemon fail to link on
macOS ("Undefined symbols").

Give it a weak definition that handles nothing instead.
system/panda-embed.c's strong definition replaces it wherever it is linked
(every system binary and libqemu-system-*.so), on both linkers.

SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later
Origin: new
---
 qapi/qmp-dispatch.c | 19 +++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/qapi/qmp-dispatch.c b/qapi/qmp-dispatch.c
index 76ea20c6a5a4b62a77cdd017951d21fa650d85ef..d780f8dcbbb14f0976699c96163dc015fb4e950f 100644
--- a/qapi/qmp-dispatch.c
+++ b/qapi/qmp-dispatch.c
@@ -26,13 +26,20 @@
 #include "qemu/main-loop.h"
 
 /*
- * Penguin QMP hook. Declared as a weak symbol so that binaries which do not
- * link system/panda-embed.c (e.g. qemu-nbd, qemu-storage-daemon) still link; the
- * pointer is NULL at runtime there and the hook is skipped.
+ * The embedding API's QMP hook. A weak default that handles nothing, so
+ * binaries which do not link system/panda-embed.c (e.g. qemu-nbd,
+ * qemu-storage-daemon) still link; panda-embed.c's strong definition replaces
+ * it where it is linked.  A weak
+ * *definition* rather than a weak reference: Mach-O's linker refuses an
+ * undefined weak reference that nothing provides.
  */
+bool panda_handle_qmp(const char *command, const char *args, char **result);
 __attribute__((weak)) bool panda_handle_qmp(const char *command,
                                             const char *args,
-                                            char **result);
+                                            char **result)
+{
+    return false;
+}
 
 Visitor *qobject_input_visitor_new_qmp(QObject *obj)
 {
@@ -189,8 +196,8 @@ QDict *coroutine_mixed_fn qmp_dispatch(const QmpCommandList *cmds, QObject *requ
     cmd = qmp_find_command(cmds, command);
     if (cmd == NULL) {
         /* --- EMBEDDING QMP HOOK START --- */
-        /* Only present when system/panda-embed.c is linked (not in qemu-nbd). */
-        if (panda_handle_qmp) {
+        /* Handles nothing unless system/panda-embed.c is linked (not in qemu-nbd). */
+        {
             char *hook_result = NULL;
             QDict *hook_args;
             GString *hook_args_json;
